# XSH fegetexceptflag(), fesetexceptflag()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every exception macro is optional (XBD <fenv.h>): a test that uses one is
# NOTINUSE when it is not defined. The stored representation is
# implementation-defined, so tests only hand it back to the same functions.

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.001
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       fegetexceptflag() returns zero when it stores the state of the flag
           of each exception the implementation defines.
test       t/001-get-return.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.002
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       fegetexceptflag() only reads the flags: a raised exception stays
           raised and a clear one stays clear.
test       t/002-get-no-change.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.003
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       fesetexceptflag() returns zero for a value stored by
           fegetexceptflag() for at least the same exceptions.
test       t/003-set-return.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.004
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       fesetexceptflag() sets an exception flag that was set when its state
           was stored, even though it was cleared in between.
test       t/004-set-restores-set.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.005
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       fesetexceptflag() puts a flag that was clear when stored back to
           clear, even though the exception was raised in between, and the call
           raises no other exception.
test       t/005-set-restores-clear.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.006
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       fesetexceptflag() changes only the flags named by its excepts
           argument: a different exception that is raised stays raised.
test       t/006-set-subset.c

assertion  XSH.fegetexceptflag.007
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fegetexceptflag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       fesetexceptflag() with an excepts argument of zero returns zero and
           leaves the flags as they were.
test       t/007-set-zero.c
